  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =A{e}^{-3(0)}+B{e}^{0}+2(0){e}^{0} \\\\ 4 & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=-3A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}+2{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=2$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =-3A{e}^{-3(0)}+B{e}^{0}+2(0){e}^{0}+2{e}^{0} \\\\ 2 & =-3A+B+2 \\\\ 0 & =-3A+B \\\\ B & =3A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=4 \\\\ B=3A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,B=3.$\n\nFinally, since $A=1$ and $B=3,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}+3{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}\n$$",
